/sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-4111993-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>4111993</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6063788-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>6063788</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-8164496-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>8164496</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9327789-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9327789</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1038628A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HANAWA KENZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUI MINING &amp; SMELTING CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANAGI KIYOTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANAWA, KENZO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUI MINING &amp; SMELTING COMPANY, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGI, KIYOTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HANAWA KENZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANAGI KIYOTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANAWA, KENZO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGI, KIYOTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Unleaded solder powder capable of preventing oxidation with time of powder surface and a production method therefor. When electronic apparatuses using a tin-lead solder are disposed of as general industrial wastes and exposed to the atmospheric environment, a lead component in the solder elutes to give adverse effects on human bodies; this has accelerated the development of a tin-zinc unleaded solder. The tin-zinc solder, however, poses problems, such as a strong susceptibility to oxidation, a very poor wettability and occurrence of large number of voids. Unleaded solder powder produced by forming, on the surface of solder alloy powder mainly comprising tin-zinc or tin-zinc-bismuth but not containing lead, an organometallic compound of malonic acid and metals in the solder alloy powder; and a production method therefor.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une poudre à souder sans plomb capable de prévenir l'oxydation progressive de sa surface. L'invention concerne également le procédé de production de cette poudre. Les appareils électroniques utilisant une soudure étain-plomb sont généralement jetés comme des déchets industriels et donc exposés à l'environnement, le constituant plomb de la soudure étant entraîné par élution et provoquant des effets nocifs sur le corps humain. Ce phénomène a donc accéléré l'élaboration d'une soudure étain-zinc sans plomb, laquelle est néanmoins largement sujette à l'oxydation, affiche une mauvaise mouillabilité, et présente un grand nombre de vides. Cette invention concerne donc une poudre à souder sans plomb que l'on produit en formant un composé organométallique à base d'acide malonique et de métaux sur la surface d'une poudre d'alliage de soudage, qui renferme essentiellement de l'étain et du zinc ou de l'étain, du zinc, et du bismuth, tout en étant exempte de plomb. L'invention concerne enfin le procédé de production de cette poudre.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>